# The build context is the REPO ROOT even though the Dockerfile lives in
# packages/solver-app — a pnpm workspace image needs the lockfile, the workspace
# manifest and every packages/*. So these patterns are root-relative.
#
# `**/` on the two build outputs rather than a bare name: the app's own build
# output is now packages/solver-app/dist, one of twelve, and a host copy of any
# of them entering the context is worse than useless — tsc is incremental, so a
# stale dist/.tsbuildinfo can make the image's own build emit nothing at all.
**/node_modules
**/dist
.data
.env
*.log
.git
docs
test
.github
